1
00:04:28,235 --> 00:04:34,235
...TO FIND THE MISSING EVIDENCE THAT WILL PROVE HIS INNOCENCE...

2
00:08:56,470 --> 00:09:02,470
The Last Chance is a drama film directed by Thomas Bentley.

3
00:13:24,705 --> 00:13:30,705
Alan Burmister leaves Devon on a secret gun-running expedition immediately after his engagement to Mary Perrin is
announced; he returns at Christmas to find himself accused of the murder of Ivor Connel, a moneylender.

4
00:17:52,941 --> 00:17:58,941
Mary's father had always hoped that his daughter would
marry John Worrall, a rising barrister.

5
00:22:21,176 --> 00:22:27,176
Worrall is briefed for the defence, but when he loses the case and Alan is condemned to penal servitude for life,
no one but the judge realises that he has not made use of the best piece of defence evidence...

6
00:26:49,411 --> 00:26:55,411
Mary Perrin, played by Judy Kelly.

7
00:31:17,647 --> 00:31:23,647
Alan Burmister, played by Frank Leighton.

8
00:35:45,882 --> 00:35:51,882
John Worrall, played by Wyndham Goldie.

9
00:40:14,117 --> 00:40:20,117
Judge Croyle, played by Aubrey Mallalieu.

10
00:44:42,352 --> 00:44:48,352
Michael Worrall, played by Billy Milton.

11
00:49:10,588 --> 00:49:16,588
Mr. Perrin, played by Laurence Hanray.

12
00:53:38,823 --> 00:53:44,823
The Last Chance is a 1937 British drama film directed by Thomas Bentley and
starring Frank Leighton, Judy Kelly and Laurence Hanray.

13
00:58:07,058 --> 00:58:13,058
Its plot involves a gunrunner who makes a jail break in order to
gather evidence to prove he is innocent of murder.

14
01:02:35,294 --> 01:02:41,294
It was made as a supporting feature at British
International Pictures' second studio at Welwyn.

15
01:07:03,529 --> 01:07:09,529
The film's sets were designed by the art director Duncan Sutherland.

16
01:11:31,764 --> 01:11:37,764
The tone is emotional.
